WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.080
When the Hou Jing Rebellion broke out, the elderly Emperor Wu of Liang was trapped inside Taicheng in Jiankang, unable to escape.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:12.734
Rebel troops besieged the city from outside, and everyone inside was filled with anxiety.

00:00:13.084 --> 00:00:20.044
The food in the city gradually ran out, until even the emperor's dining table held only empty bowls and plates.

00:00:20.394 --> 00:00:27.738
The emperor, over eighty years old, had lost his freedom; all day he gazed out of the window and could only sigh helplessly.

00:00:28.088 --> 00:00:38.456
In the year 549, Emperor Wu of Liang passed away in Taicheng, ending a legendary and long life.

00:00:38.806 --> 00:00:46.558
This emperor, who had reigned for nearly half a century, met a tragic end in his later years because politics had spun out of control.

00:00:46.908 --> 00:00:55.212
His passing marked the end of the Liang dynasty's golden age, and Jiangnan fell into a long period of turmoil.

00:00:55.562 --> 00:01:00.506
People longed for the peaceful days of the past and hoped that peace would return.

